            "review_title": "Review at Vua Vit Co Lan Ba",
            "review_text": "JSTrip_77\nSarajevo, Bosnia and Herzegovina1194 contributions\n0\nBustling Lunchtime\nOct 2018 • Solo\nIf you're looking for a bit of flavor beyond the more well-appointed restaurants but don't necessarily want street food, Lan Ba is a pretty good option. I had a delicious duck salad (with sliced mango) today and really enjoyed it. The place was packed which is one of the reasons I picked it. In fact, there wasn't a seat for me so the hostess set up a little table just for me. While it took a bit longer to get my food than I'd hoped or expected, the restaurant staff was running around working very hard - AND they had a large work party in a separate room that seemed to be running them ragged! The staff was really nice and my minimal Vietnamese wasn't even necessary. Pointing worked just fine. \n\nThis restaurant is located in close proximity to the American Center and is a place that I'd certainly return in the future. They seem to offer a menu focused on poultry but also have meat and vegetarian options.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten October 19, 2018",
